Q: Query deeply nested document with dynamic key A: <p>I think it will be difficult with a <code>find</code> but an <a href="https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/aggregation-pipeline/#std-label-aggregation-pipeline" rel="nofollow noreferrer">aggregation pipeline</a> could do the job.
What about this one:</p>
<pre><code>db.leagues.aggregate([
  { $match: { _id: &quot;693ae6dc320b2bb92635361e&quot; } },
  {
    $project: {
      cards: {
        $filter: {
          input: &quot;$cards&quot;,
          as: &quot;card&quot;,
          cond: { $eq: [ &quot;$$this._id&quot;, &quot;600056266&quot; ] }
        }
      }
    }
  },
  { $unwind: &quot;$cards&quot; },
  {
    $project: {
      users: {
        $filter: {
          input: &quot;$cards.users&quot;,
          cond: { $eq: [ &quot;$$this._id&quot;, &quot;EafXiJktdKSM45OcnniU4gpcGWc2&quot; ] }
        }
      }
    }
  },
  { $unwind: &quot;$users&quot; },
  { $replaceWith: &quot;$users.vote&quot; }
])
</code></pre>
<p><a href="https://mongoplayground.net/p/O56FHRFkQmK" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Mongo Playground</a></p>
<p>You may set first stage to</p>
<pre><code>  {
    $match: {
      _id: &quot;693ae6dc320b2bb92635361e&quot;,
      &quot;cards._id&quot;: &quot;600056266&quot;,
      &quot;cards.users._id&quot;: &quot;EafXiJktdKSM45OcnniU4gpcGWc2&quot;
    }
  }
</code></pre>
<p>It may give better performance. It returns only the documents which will return a result, i.e. the following stages get only documents which let to an output.</p>
